{
 "schema": "v8.delta/2",
 "phase": "v8 Phase 6: exposure-local positive crypto authority - the known-crypto list is ticker-level knowledge and is bound to at most one price-coherent exposure of its ticker; several candidates stay UNVERIFIED (TICKER_CRYPTO_EXPOSURE_UNBOUND), never AMBIGUOUS; tradfi, ambiguous, check-blocked and unpriced exposures are never candidates (v8.identity/4)",
 "base": {
  "sha": "f7aa7f6d318f4dfcd84c74df27d38314e4349208",
  "tree": "aff2774ce726c10711ec3276c59e6dec81b453e8",
  "golden": "tests/fixtures/v8/legacy_parity_golden_phase5.json",
  "note": "production main after the Phase 5 merge (PR #16); its fixture golden is the Phase 5 branch golden"
 },
 "head_golden": "tests/fixtures/v8/legacy_parity_golden_phase6.json",
 "counterfactual_projection": "exclude_without_execution_identity",
 "rules": {
  "TICKER_CRYPTO_EXPOSURE_UNBOUND": "v8.identity/4: the known-crypto list says one crypto asset exists under a ticker, not which of its price-separated exposures that asset is. After every piece of contract evidence classified what it can (tradfi, ambiguous, direct crypto), and exposures blocked by a failed exposure check and unpriced exposures are set aside, the list is bound to the one candidate left; with more than one candidate nothing chooses (no volume, venue count, open interest, age or majority vote) and every candidate is UNVERIFIED (not AMBIGUOUS: no economic evidence conflicts). The coin stays in the universe (discovery) and loses crypto execution identity.",
  "UNBOUND_NOT_COUNTED_AS_CRYPTO": "A DEX's count of crypto markets counts only markets admitted with crypto execution identity: the markets of a known-crypto coin whose list authority could not be bound to one exposure are no longer counted.",
  "UNVERIFIED_LISTED_SEPARATELY": "The radar publishes identity-unverified coins in coverage.unverified, not among the non-crypto (tradfi) exclusions in coverage.tradfi: unknown is not tradfi. The counterfactual hands every coin without crypto execution identity to the base code as tradfi (its only exclusion); HEAD lists the unverified ones apart (FAKE07 joins them).",
  "IDENTITY_VERSION_BUMP": "Entry-time identity provenance of a paper trade opened in this run records the identity version of the authority that allowed it: v8.identity/4. Written once; a trade opened under v8.identity/2 or /3 keeps its proof and stays qualified (no hindsight). Every other trade value is unchanged."
 },
 "universe": [
  {
   "ticker": "FAKE07",
   "field": "execution_identity",
   "base": true,
   "head": false,
   "rule": "TICKER_CRYPTO_EXPOSURE_UNBOUND",
   "why": "FAKE07 is on the fixture world's known-crypto list. Its priced contracts form two price-coherent exposures: FAKE07#1 (Hyperliquid FAKE07, Variational FAKE07) and FAKE07#2 (dYdX FAKE07-USD, 30% away). Neither carries economic evidence and neither is blocked by an exposure check, so both are binding candidates: the ticker list names one crypto asset and cannot tell which exposure it is (nothing chooses by volume or venue count). v8.identity/3 verified both from the list; v8.identity/4: both UNVERIFIED, TICKER_CRYPTO_EXPOSURE_UNBOUND, ticker_authority.result UNBOUND_MULTIPLE_CANDIDATES. The coin record is unchanged (rule 5: the record of its UNVERIFIED exposures; the legacy price check drops the dYdX market as before)."
  },
  {
